the compensation that should have been covered by social security

285
00:15:11,320 --> 00:15:13,580
will all have to be paid by their law firm.

286
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:16,080
Then Liu Xincheng definitely won't be happy about it.

287
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,480
It's a lot of money.

288
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:21,840
That day at

289
00:15:21,840 --> 00:15:22,400
the ICU

290
00:15:22,400 --> 00:15:23,240
entrance.

291
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:25,600
This Liu Xincheng looks a bit strange.

292
00:15:26,320 --> 00:15:28,180
Sister-in-law, we can't give up.

293
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:29,600
As long as we can save Xiaotian,

294
00:15:29,600 --> 00:15:30,860
money is not a problem.

295
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:33,160
I regret to inform all relatives and friends

296
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:34,220
that the patient's

297
00:15:34,440 --> 00:15:36,240
heart has just stopped beating.

298
00:15:38,040 --> 00:15:39,000
I didn't expect this.

299
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,800
He timed it perfectly, didn't he?

300
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:42,360
He just wanted to drag it out past 48 hours

301
00:15:42,360 --> 00:15:43,040
so the old squad leader

302
00:15:43,040 --> 00:15:44,640
wouldn't meet the conditions for work injury compensation.

303
00:15:44,640 --> 00:15:46,970
Isn't he just a bad guy exploiting the law?

304
00:15:47,400 --> 00:15:49,160
We absolutely can't let him succeed.

305
00:15:49,160 --> 00:15:50,120
Let's do this.

306
00:15:50,760 --> 00:15:52,360
We'll split into two groups.

307
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:54,600
You two go to the hospital tomorrow

308
00:15:54,760 --> 00:15:56,280
and carefully investigate

309
00:15:56,280 --> 00:15:58,760
the details of the old squad leader's rescue.

310
00:15:58,760 --> 00:15:59,440
Sister-in-law said

311
00:15:59,440 --> 00:16:02,440
the old squad leader lost his phone the day he fell ill.

312
00:16:02,520 --> 00:16:03,580
I'll go look for it.

313
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:07,080
There's a high chance evidence of his work is on his phone.

314
00:16:07,080 --> 00:16:08,240
I'll go with you.

315
00:16:08,680 --> 00:16:09,280
Okay.

316
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:16,730
What's up? Is something wrong?

317
00:16:17,560 --> 00:16:19,240
No, just navigating.

318
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:21,850
Aren't we going to the hospital tomorrow?

319
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:25,040
Here you go.

320
00:16:25,040 --> 00:16:25,970
Okay, thank you.

321
00:16:26,960 --> 00:16:28,290
Got it, sister-in-law.

322
00:16:37,160 --> 00:16:39,400
This Yang Fan should be

323
00:16:39,400 --> 00:16:41,680
the last client the old squad leader saw.

324
00:16:45,960 --> 00:16:46,520
Hello?

325
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,560
Hello, Mr. Tian.

326
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,280
I finally got through to you.

327
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:51,880
The gift you ordered at our store

328
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:52,960
is ready.

329
00:16:53,200 --> 00:16:55,560
You can come pick it up anytime today.

330
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:57,400
Hello?

331
00:16:58,080 --> 00:16:58,960
Thank you.

332
00:17:01,920 --> 00:17:02,600
Tomorrow

333
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:05,260
is my wedding anniversary with Lao Tian.

334
00:17:06,200 --> 00:17:08,160
I told him not to waste money.

335
00:17:08,960 --> 00:17:10,220
He's so busy with work.

336
00:17:10,720 --> 00:17:12,240
Why did he even buy a gift?

337
00:17:22,560 --> 00:17:23,359
Director Liu.

338
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,359
The work injury certification from the Human Resources and Social Security Bureau is out.

339
00:17:26,359 --> 00:17:30,090
I hope you can compensate Lawyer Tian's family as soon as possible.

340
00:17:30,120 --> 00:17:32,000
Lawyer Xiao, look.

341
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:34,760
It says brain death here.

342
00:17:35,520 --> 00:17:37,120
We are all in the legal profession,

343
00:17:37,120 --> 00:17:38,480
so you must know

344
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:42,180
that in practice, the law recognizes cardiopulmonary death.

345
00:17:42,280 --> 00:17:44,960
Brain death is only a medical certification.

346
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,120
Director Liu.

347
00:17:46,760 --> 00:17:48,040
In judicial practice,

348
00:17:48,320 --> 00:17:49,980
there are already precedents

349
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,840
using brain death to determine death.

350
00:17:51,840 --> 00:17:53,280
If we can't negotiate,

351
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:54,740
then let's go to court.

352
00:17:55,640 --> 00:17:56,440
Director Liu.

353
00:17:56,880 --> 00:17:58,280
Since we are both in the legal profession,

354
00:17:58,280 --> 00:17:58,840
there is no need

355
00:17:58,840 --> 00:18:00,560
to make this matter so complicated.

356
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:01,600
Lawyer Tian has been at your firm,

357
00:18:01,600 --> 00:18:03,400
serving diligently for so long.

358
00:18:03,760 --> 00:18:05,560
He deserves this compensation.

359
00:18:05,560 --> 00:18:06,160
Lawyer Li.

360
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:10,040
My firm isn't as wealthy as your Honghu.

361
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,240
I can't let Tian alone

362
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:14,040
take my firm's profits from the past few years.

363
00:18:14,040 --> 00:18:15,320
If we fill it all in,

364
00:18:15,760 --> 00:18:17,760
how will the other lawyers survive?

365
00:18:18,160 --> 00:18:19,420
You're exaggerating.

366
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:20,690
Look, Director Liu.

367
00:18:21,200 --> 00:18:22,600
This is your law firm's win rate

368
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:23,720
and caseload.

369
00:18:24,280 --> 00:18:26,280
The profit should be more than this.

370
00:18:27,880 --> 00:18:30,520
It's just for marketing purposes.

371
00:18:30,760 --> 00:18:32,480
Then that's data falsification.

372
00:18:32,480 --> 00:18:33,160
In the past two years,

373
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,760
the Justice Bureau and the Bar Association

374
00:18:34,760 --> 00:18:36,560
have been cracking down on this behavior.

375
00:18:36,560 --> 00:18:38,400
The law firm really doesn't have that much money.

376
00:18:38,400 --> 00:18:39,320
If we did...

377
00:18:39,320 --> 00:18:40,440
He's been with me for so many years.

378
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:41,760
I don't want to treat him unfairly.

379
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:43,240
You don't want to treat him unfairly?

380
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:45,320
Then why didn't you provide him with social security?

381
00:18:45,320 --> 00:18:46,600
You don't want to treat him unfairly.

382
00:18:46,600 --> 00:18:49,040
Yet you make him work over 15 hours a day.

383
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:51,480
Do you treat him as a human being or a consumable?

384
00:18:51,480 --> 00:18:53,560
Isn't the whole industry like this?

385
00:18:53,840 --> 00:18:55,320
The competition is so fierce.

386
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:57,480
Who isn't working from dawn to dusk?

387
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,700
Even me, the director of the law firm.

388
00:18:59,800 --> 00:19:02,320
I also have to run around to find cases,

389
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:05,480
and be called over to entertain clients anytime, anywhere.

390
00:19:05,480 --> 00:19:06,840
I'm used to it.

391
00:19:06,840 --> 00:19:08,300
What kind of habit is that?

392
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:10,040
Isn't it a bad practice?

393
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,600
Shouldn't we unite

394
00:19:11,600 --> 00:19:13,040
and change this toxic culture?

395
00:19:13,040 --> 00:19:14,720
Why are you compromising with it?

396
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:15,920
Lawyer Xiao is right.

397
00:19:16,080 --> 00:19:17,360
Unhealthy unspoken industry rules

398
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:18,960
should indeed be boycotted.

399
00:19:19,240 --> 00:19:20,760
If even a law firm cannot

400
00:19:20,760 --> 00:19:21,920
respect the Labor Law,

401
00:19:21,920 --> 00:19:23,400
how can we make clients believe

402
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:26,460
that the law will protect the lives of ordinary people?

403
00:19:27,840 --> 00:19:28,680
Director Liu.

404
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:30,760
I have a proposal.

405
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:32,960
We can pay this compensation

406
00:19:33,120 --> 00:19:35,720
in installments

407
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:37,520
to Lawyer Tian's family.

408
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:41,080
This way, your finances won't take a huge hit.

409
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:43,640
Honghu will have some outsourced cases.

410
00:19:44,080 --> 00:19:46,410
I can help connect you when the time comes.

411
00:19:50,720 --> 00:19:52,320
Thanks to you, Lawyer Li.

412
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:54,760
Because you prepared a trump card in advance,

413
00:19:54,760 --> 00:19:56,690
the negotiation went so smoothly.

414
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:57,610
Impressive.

415
00:19:58,360 --> 00:19:59,720
That's not entirely accurate.

416
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,520
Didn't we prepare it together?

417
00:20:02,840 --> 00:20:03,880
All this time,

418
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:07,850
thank you for being with me.

419
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:14,210
Isn't that what I should do?

420
00:20:14,840 --> 00:20:17,600
Otherwise, how could we join forces?

421
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:20,960
You still remember that?

422
00:20:22,480 --> 00:20:23,520
I never forgot.

423
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,760
That director of Qianyue Law Firm,

424
00:20:34,760 --> 00:20:36,600
he didn't want to pay compensation from the start.

425
00:20:36,600 --> 00:20:37,640
He even dragged out the rescue time

426
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:39,760
past the standard for work-related injury recognition.

427
00:20:39,760 --> 00:20:40,840
How shameless.

428
00:20:40,960 --> 00:20:41,640
Yes.

429
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:42,880
Do you need my help?

430
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:44,840
That won't be necessary.

431
00:20:44,840 --> 00:20:47,700
The director and Lawyer Li have already handled it.

432
00:20:47,880 --> 00:20:50,280
Then just tell me the conclusion next time.

433
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:51,640
Uncle, you told me

434
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,440
to tell you the details of the process.

435
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:54,520
I was just saying. Alright, alright.

436
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:55,360
Anyway,

437
00:20:55,360 --> 00:20:57,800
no matter what happens in the law firm from now on,

438
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:59,280
you report to me first.

439
00:20:59,920 --> 00:21:00,600
Okay.

440
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:01,560
Keep that in mind.

441
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,400
Come, come. Please.

442
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:06,850
I'm telling you, eat well, drink well, and wash well.

443
00:21:07,160 --> 00:21:08,640
Uncle, it's Liu Xincheng.

444
00:21:12,040 --> 00:21:12,840
Director Liu.

445
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:16,520
You know me?

446
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:18,360
Important people have short memories.

447
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:20,960
We met at Lawyer Tian's funeral.

448
00:21:21,280 --> 00:21:22,520
Look at me.

449
00:21:22,520 --> 00:21:23,320
My memory is so bad.

450
00:21:23,320 --> 00:21:24,840
Go, enjoy yourselves.

451
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:26,120
Okay, please go upstairs, you two.

452
00:21:26,120 --> 00:21:27,760
Goodbye. Let's go.

453
00:21:29,520 --> 00:21:30,780
I know him, Brother Hu.

454
00:21:32,280 --> 00:21:33,400
Find Director Liu

455
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:35,120
the strongest bath attendant.

456
00:21:35,120 --> 00:21:37,400
He's a dirty guy.

457
00:21:37,400 --> 00:21:38,660
His heart is not clean.

458
00:21:38,840 --> 00:21:39,560
Understood.

459
00:21:39,560 --> 00:21:40,360
I'll go myself.

460
00:21:40,360 --> 00:21:41,920
I'll scrub his soul clean.

461
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,320
I'll let him know what pain is.

462
00:21:43,320 --> 00:21:44,380
Sting him to death.

463
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:54,520
Ms. Xiao.

464
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:56,200
I beg you, please help me.

465
00:21:56,240 --> 00:21:57,720
No one believes me now,

466
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:59,960
and no one dares to take Wangang's case.

467
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:01,800
I'm sorry.

468
00:22:02,120 --> 00:22:03,600
I've said all I have to say.

469
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:04,560
I can't help you.

470
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:05,960
Did you hear that?

471
00:22:05,960 --> 00:22:07,720
Our law firm can't take your case.

472
00:22:07,720 --> 00:22:09,980
If you come again, we'll call the police.

473
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:25,120
We came to see you.

474
00:22:29,360 --> 00:22:32,240
Longnv and Lawyer Li

475
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:35,780
helped you apply for work-related injury certification.

476
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:39,280
The compensation has come through.

477
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:41,080
My son and I

478
00:22:41,200 --> 00:22:43,400
will be financially secure from now on.

479
00:22:44,200 --> 00:22:45,240
Rest assured.

480
00:22:46,360 --> 00:22:47,480
I won't break down.

481
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:51,100
I will live a good life for you.

482
00:22:59,440 --> 00:23:00,440
Old squad leader.

483
00:23:01,920 --> 00:23:02,840
Rest assured.

484
00:23:24,920 --> 00:23:26,520
Excuse me for interrupting.

485
00:23:27,560 --> 00:23:28,440
I am the last client

486
00:23:28,440 --> 00:23:30,170
Lawyer Tian saw before he died.

487
00:23:35,480 --> 00:23:38,360
Actually, I owe Lawyer Tian a lot.

488
00:23:39,360 --> 00:23:41,120
At first, I chose Lawyer Tian.

489
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:44,080
Lawyer Tian, this is the termination of the contract.

490
00:23:44,080 --> 00:23:45,080
Later, I heard

491
00:23:45,160 --> 00:23:47,000
it took him three years to pass the bar exam.

492
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:49,280
I thought he probably wasn't capable enough,

493
00:23:49,280 --> 00:23:50,480
so I changed lawyers.

494
00:23:50,840 --> 00:23:51,840
Please stay.

495
00:23:51,880 --> 00:23:53,010
No need to see me out.

496
00:23:55,080 --> 00:23:56,080
But that lawyer

497
00:23:56,080 --> 00:23:57,840
was obviously not as responsible as Lawyer Tian.

498
00:23:57,840 --> 00:23:58,920
Have you waited long, Mr. Yang?

499
00:23:58,920 --> 00:24:00,380
I went back to Lawyer Tian.

500
00:24:00,920 --> 00:24:02,960
But Lawyer Tian's attitude towards my case

501
00:24:02,960 --> 00:24:04,220
hadn't changed at all.

502
00:24:04,560 --> 00:24:06,840
I even asked him how he did it.

503
00:24:07,720 --> 00:24:08,600
What did he say?

504
00:24:09,600 --> 00:24:11,120
He recited an oath to me.

505
00:24:12,080 --> 00:24:13,360
But I remember after he finished,

506
00:24:13,360 --> 00:24:15,420
he smiled good-naturedly and told me

507
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:17,320
that the oath didn't teach him

508
00:24:17,320 --> 00:24:18,920
to get angry with the client.

509
00:24:31,240 --> 00:24:32,280
Since I started practicing,

510
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:34,540
it was the first time I got hit by a client.

511
00:24:34,560 --> 00:24:37,200
I felt wronged and angry at the time.

512
00:24:37,680 --> 00:24:40,000
But after calming down, I reflected

513
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:42,600
that maybe I didn't emphasize the consequences of losing the case

514
00:24:42,600 --> 00:24:44,720
enough.

515
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:46,960
In the morning, I accompanied my supervising lawyer

516
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:49,200
to the detention center to pick up our client.

517
00:24:49,200 --> 00:24:52,280
As soon as he came out, he hugged the lawyer and sobbed,

518
00:24:52,280 --> 00:24:54,240
saying it was like being reborn.

519
00:24:54,640 --> 00:24:57,120
This was the first criminal case I encountered,

520
00:24:57,120 --> 00:24:59,720
and I deeply felt the importance of a good lawyer

521
00:24:59,720 --> 00:25:02,160
to a client's fate.

522
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:03,120
Today,

523
00:25:03,280 --> 00:25:05,560
I finally passed the bar exam

524
00:25:05,600 --> 00:25:07,960
and became an intern lawyer.

525
00:25:08,240 --> 00:25:10,680
I once read in a book

526
00:25:10,720 --> 00:25:13,320
that someone described the medical profession like this:

527
00:25:13,320 --> 00:25:16,040
To cure sometimes, to relieve often,

528
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,400
to comfort always.

529
00:25:17,880 --> 00:25:20,000
I think lawyers should be the same.

530
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,680
I volunteer to dedicate myself to the political and legal cause,

531
00:25:21,680 --> 00:25:24,000
love the motherland, be loyal to the people,

532
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:25,760
uphold the humanistic spirit,

533
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,600
and relentlessly pursue truth.

534
00:25:27,600 --> 00:25:29,320
To wield the sword of justice,

535
00:25:29,320 --> 00:25:31,120
hold the scales of fairness,

536
00:25:31,120 --> 00:25:32,880
eliminate evil from the world,

537
00:25:32,880 --> 00:25:34,880
and protect the sanctity of the law.

538
00:25:34,880 --> 00:25:38,600
I will strive for the construction of socialist rule of law for my whole life,

539
00:25:38,600 --> 00:25:40,040
unwaveringly.

540
00:25:40,040 --> 00:25:41,840
Oath taker, Tian Yonghou.

541
00:26:10,800 --> 00:26:11,560
Today,

542
00:26:11,680 --> 00:26:13,960
I finally got my own lawyer's license.

543
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,760
Congratulations.

544
00:26:17,960 --> 00:26:19,360
So that means from now on,

545
00:26:19,600 --> 00:26:21,480
we should call you Little Lawyer Wang.

546
00:26:21,480 --> 00:26:22,800
What do you mean "Little Lawyer Wang"?

547
00:26:22,800 --> 00:26:24,920
She is officially Lawyer Wang now.

548
00:26:25,040 --> 00:26:26,720
Lawyer Wang.

549
00:26:27,960 --> 00:26:29,480
Lawyer Li, you should call her that too.

550
00:26:29,480 --> 00:26:30,210
Lawyer Wang.

551
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:32,210
You must be secretly happy.

552
00:26:33,680 --> 00:26:34,920
I'm sorry, everyone.

553
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:38,760
I don't plan to be Lawyer Wang yet.

554
00:26:40,080 --> 00:26:41,480
What do you mean?

555
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:43,890
Haven't you had enough of the internship?

556
00:26:44,360 --> 00:26:47,560
I'm going to apply to NYU School of Law

557
00:26:48,320 --> 00:26:49,560
for further studies.

558
00:26:49,560 --> 00:26:50,760
This is too sudden.

559
00:26:51,320 --> 00:26:52,840
Have you thought it through?

560
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:54,640
Although I hate to leave you all,

561
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:58,540
this is the result of my careful consideration.

562
00:27:05,160 --> 00:27:06,280
I'm very happy

563
00:27:06,600 --> 00:27:08,720
to have met you all as soon as I entered the workplace.

564
00:27:08,720 --> 00:27:10,840
But I want to take advantage of my youth

565
00:27:10,840 --> 00:27:12,800
to go out and see the world.

566
00:27:12,920 --> 00:27:14,200
Until I can figure out

567
00:27:14,200 --> 00:27:15,320
exactly what kind of lawyer

568
00:27:15,320 --> 00:27:16,280
I want to be.

569
00:27:16,760 --> 00:27:19,960
I believe you can definitely do it.

570
00:27:20,160 --> 00:27:22,720
After you've looked around,

571
00:27:23,240 --> 00:27:24,840
you're welcome back to our team.

572
00:27:24,840 --> 00:27:27,240
Don't look down on us then.

573
00:27:28,200 --> 00:27:29,260
That's hard to say.

574
00:27:31,800 --> 00:27:32,520
Bowen.

575
00:27:32,520 --> 00:27:33,800
I'm not drunk.

576
00:27:33,800 --> 00:27:34,600
Okay, okay.

577
00:27:35,360 --> 00:27:36,160
My glasses.

578
00:27:38,720 --> 00:27:39,840
Take good care of him.

579
00:27:39,840 --> 00:27:40,480
Okay, Ruoqi.

580
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:41,080
Boss.

581
00:27:41,160 --> 00:27:42,400
Hold this for him in case he throws up.

582
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:43,440
I won't see you off.

583
00:27:43,440 --> 00:27:44,440
Bye, boss. Bye, Ruoqi.

584
00:27:44,440 --> 00:27:45,160
Ruoqi.

585
00:27:45,600 --> 00:27:46,920
I will miss you.

586
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:51,080
Lawyer Li.

587
00:27:51,600 --> 00:27:53,200
We agreed I would pay for this meal.

588
00:27:53,200 --> 00:27:54,480
Why did you pay again?

589
00:27:55,960 --> 00:27:57,360
Since you graduated from Honghu

590
00:27:57,360 --> 00:27:58,440
and call me your mentor,

591
00:27:58,440 --> 00:28:00,560
it's only natural for me to treat you to a meal.

592
00:28:00,560 --> 00:28:01,560
Let's wait until you come back.

593
00:28:01,560 --> 00:28:03,160
I'll treat everyone to a meal then.

594
00:28:03,160 --> 00:28:05,000
Okay. Thank you, Mr. Li.

595
00:28:05,600 --> 00:28:06,600
Did you call a cab?

596
00:28:06,920 --> 00:28:08,440
Yes. It'll be here in a few minutes.

597
00:28:08,440 --> 00:28:10,300
Okay. I'll wait with you for a bit.

598
00:28:14,160 --> 00:28:15,680
I'm leaving anyway.

599
00:28:16,280 --> 00:28:19,120
I want to be honest with you.

600
00:28:22,840 --> 00:28:23,520
Go ahead.

601
00:28:24,640 --> 00:28:26,240
Although your name is Li Xin,

602
00:28:26,920 --> 00:28:29,200
I don't think you need to live up to it

603
00:28:29,240 --> 00:28:31,840
by being rational all the time.

604
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:33,000
When you work,

605
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:34,000
don't push yourself too hard.

606
00:28:34,000 --> 00:28:35,320
Your health is very important.

607
00:28:35,320 --> 00:28:36,080
The way you are

608
00:28:36,080 --> 00:28:38,280
makes the people close to you worry.

609
00:28:38,400 --> 00:28:39,840
And most importantly,

610
00:28:40,360 --> 00:28:42,560
don't always close your heart

611
00:28:43,160 --> 00:28:45,000
and shut everyone out.

612
00:28:47,720 --> 00:28:48,320
Okay.

613
00:28:49,320 --> 00:28:50,920
I've received your lecture.

614
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:52,280
I will reflect on it.

615
00:28:52,960 --> 00:28:54,360
Why does it sound like you're leaving

616
00:28:54,360 --> 00:28:56,600
and taking the chance to scold me?

617
00:28:56,720 --> 00:28:57,840
I'm not done yet.

618
00:28:58,800 --> 00:28:59,840
Okay, go on.

619
00:29:01,240 --> 00:29:03,170
You also have many good qualities.

620
00:29:03,240 --> 00:29:04,040
Capable,

621
00:29:05,480 --> 00:29:06,440
responsible,

622
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:07,840
principled,

623
00:29:08,320 --> 00:29:10,400
very accountable and reliable.

624
00:29:10,840 --> 00:29:11,970
I like you very much.

625
00:29:18,920 --> 00:29:19,960
Did I scare you?

626
00:29:21,200 --> 00:29:21,680
No.

627
00:29:23,040 --> 00:29:24,040
Don't be nervous.

628
00:29:24,240 --> 00:29:25,920
I don't need you to respond.

629
00:29:27,040 --> 00:29:28,120
I just think

630
00:29:28,680 --> 00:29:31,440
liking someone is a beautiful thing.

631
00:29:32,840 --> 00:29:34,170
I wanted to let you know.

632
00:29:35,560 --> 00:29:36,440
That's all.

633
00:29:39,360 --> 00:29:40,040
Thank you.

634
00:29:40,280 --> 00:29:43,360
So, can you let Lawyer Xiao

635
00:29:43,840 --> 00:29:45,200
know your feelings too?

636
00:29:48,160 --> 00:29:49,200
I can tell

637
00:29:49,640 --> 00:29:51,160
you treat Lawyer Xiao

638
00:29:51,160 --> 00:29:52,800
differently from others.

639
00:29:54,040 --> 00:29:55,320
Did you give up

640
00:29:55,560 --> 00:29:56,600
the offer in Hong Kong

641
00:29:56,600 --> 00:29:57,640
because of her?

642
00:29:58,600 --> 00:30:00,060
Your resume is excellent.

643
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:04,040
Tell me.

644
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:06,120
Why do you want to come to Honghu?

645
00:30:06,120 --> 00:30:06,720
I...

646
00:30:08,040 --> 00:30:08,800
Come in.

647
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:11,900
Director, I've finished this document.

648
00:30:14,160 --> 00:30:14,920
Li Xin.

649
00:30:15,160 --> 00:30:16,160
Why are you here?

650
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:22,050
Have you really decided to come to Honghu?

651
00:30:24,960 --> 00:30:26,600
Didn't you receive an offer

652
00:30:26,600 --> 00:30:28,130
from a big firm in Hong Kong?

653
00:30:29,680 --> 00:30:31,920
I can be the best lawyer anywhere.

654
00:30:32,600 --> 00:30:33,880
Besides, didn't we say

655
00:30:33,880 --> 00:30:36,000
we'd join forces after graduation?

656
00:30:36,400 --> 00:30:38,880
Good for you. You kept your word.

657
00:30:40,800 --> 00:30:42,330
Travel the world together.

658
00:30:42,600 --> 00:30:43,130
Let's go.

659
00:30:46,840 --> 00:30:48,320
That's obviously love.

660
00:30:48,440 --> 00:30:50,040
Why are you afraid to say it?

661
00:30:52,280 --> 00:30:54,140
If you keep hesitating like this,

662
00:30:54,560 --> 00:30:56,240
you might really lose her.

663
00:31:40,480 --> 00:31:41,360
Standing here

664
00:31:41,800 --> 00:31:42,840
to welcome me?

665
00:31:44,360 --> 00:31:45,480
Flattered?

666
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:50,800
I have something to tell you.

667
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:52,560
What a coincidence.

668
00:31:52,560 --> 00:31:54,360
I have something to tell you too.

669
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:56,250
You go first.

670
00:32:04,480 --> 00:32:06,360
I'm going to take Old Pan's case.

671
00:32:08,920 --> 00:32:12,320
While handling the old squad leader's funeral,

672
00:32:13,200 --> 00:32:14,400
I kept thinking about

673
00:32:15,200 --> 00:32:17,440
what we used to say when we were kids:

674
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,920
"Wielding the sword of justice."

675
00:32:18,920 --> 00:32:20,450
What are we wielding it for?

676
00:32:21,560 --> 00:32:22,920
Then I figured it out.

677
00:32:23,280 --> 00:32:24,360
Isn't it to

678
00:32:24,920 --> 00:32:26,560
help those who suffer injustice

679
00:32:26,560 --> 00:32:27,760
get justice?

680
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:29,730
This is my original intention.

681
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:30,880
I can't say that

682
00:32:30,880 --> 00:32:32,640
just because Old Pan stood me up once,

683
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:34,440
I forgot my original intention.

684
00:32:34,760 --> 00:32:36,440
Now that Old Pan is facing injustice,

685
00:32:36,440 --> 00:32:38,880
I have to wield the sword of justice for him.

686
00:32:39,760 --> 00:32:40,440
Right?

687
00:32:45,080 --> 00:32:45,800
I

688
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:48,690
respect your decision.

689
00:32:49,800 --> 00:32:51,120
Since you've already drawn your sword,

690
00:32:51,120 --> 00:32:53,120
I have no choice but to draw my blade.

691
00:32:53,480 --> 00:32:56,120
Let's be opponents one more time.

692
00:32:57,080 --> 00:32:58,340
Bring it on, opponent.

693
00:33:28,320 --> 00:33:29,780
Thank you, Attorney Xiao.

694
00:33:29,880 --> 00:33:31,080
Thank you so much.

695
00:33:31,240 --> 00:33:34,840
I really didn't expect you to take my case.

696
00:33:34,840 --> 00:33:35,770
You're welcome.

697
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:38,320
Well, let's go check out the situation.

698
00:33:39,080 --> 00:33:41,200
Last year, the shrimp farming failed.

699
00:33:41,200 --> 00:33:43,400
This year, I wanted to go big,

700
00:33:43,760 --> 00:33:46,200
so I invested twice as much money as last year.

701
00:33:46,200 --> 00:33:47,200
To get this loan,

702
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:49,080
I even mortgaged my house.

703
00:33:49,520 --> 00:33:50,720
I never expected this.

704
00:33:50,720 --> 00:33:54,160
All this money has gone down the drain.

705
00:33:55,080 --> 00:33:55,760
Look.

706
00:34:00,080 --> 00:34:02,410
Are other farmers experiencing this too?

707
00:34:02,680 --> 00:34:04,680
Anyone farming in these waters

708
00:34:05,120 --> 00:34:06,280
has suffered.

709
00:34:06,280 --> 00:34:08,440
Now they're acting just like last year.

710
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:10,159
If I win, they'll sue.

711
00:34:10,560 --> 00:34:12,280
If I lose, they'll lay low.

712
00:34:12,440 --> 00:34:14,239
Those shrimp stink.

713
00:34:14,440 --> 00:34:16,480
Why haven't you scooped them out if they've been dead so long?

714
00:34:16,480 --> 00:34:19,719
We don't dare scoop them out until we get an explanation.

715
00:34:20,920 --> 00:34:22,239
Have you talked to Wangang?

716
00:34:22,239 --> 00:34:23,159
I did.

717
00:34:23,360 --> 00:34:24,489
They won't admit it.

718
00:34:25,040 --> 00:34:27,880
The situation this year is the same as last year.

719
00:34:28,080 --> 00:34:29,409
I won't bother anymore.

720
00:34:29,600 --> 00:34:30,719
Just let Wangang and the others

721
00:34:30,719 --> 00:34:32,440
compensate us according to last year's standard.

722
00:34:32,440 --> 00:34:33,239
Sorry, Mr. Pan.

723
00:34:33,239 --> 00:34:35,040
I have to correct your wording.

724
00:34:35,600 --> 00:34:38,120
Last year, Wangang didn't call it compensation.

725
00:34:38,120 --> 00:34:39,719
Instead, out of humanitarianism,

726
00:34:39,719 --> 00:34:41,040
they contacted a third-party company

727
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:42,560
to buy all your shrimp.

728
00:34:47,080 --> 00:34:48,520
This is just an ordinary

729
00:34:48,520 --> 00:34:50,480
third-party shrimp purchase contract.

730
00:34:50,480 --> 00:34:53,480
Wangang indeed didn't admit to the sewage discharge.

731
00:35:01,000 --> 00:35:01,680
Mr. Wan.

732
00:35:02,440 --> 00:35:03,720
Last year's pipeline damage

733
00:35:03,720 --> 00:35:04,920
was just an accident.

734
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:06,720
This year, we specifically added

735
00:35:06,720 --> 00:35:08,080
several quality control measures.

736
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:11,080
I can guarantee there will be absolutely no problems.

737
00:35:13,520 --> 00:35:14,200
Mr. Wan,

738
00:35:14,720 --> 00:35:16,720
there's a document you need to sign.

739
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:19,050
No rush. We'll talk after the meeting.

740
00:35:25,840 --> 00:35:28,160
You don't need to wait. Go do your work.

741
00:35:28,400 --> 00:35:29,880
It's such an important meeting.

742
00:35:29,880 --> 00:35:31,140
I want to participate.

743
00:35:31,200 --> 00:35:32,760
Just in case I can be of help.

744
00:35:32,800 --> 00:35:33,800
Please continue.

745
00:35:35,520 --> 00:35:36,720
Well, no matter what,

746
00:35:36,720 --> 00:35:38,440
since it has already happened,

747
00:35:38,440 --> 00:35:40,480
Let's figure out a way to solve it quickly.

748
00:35:40,480 --> 00:35:42,600
I think Attorney Li's method last year

749
00:35:42,600 --> 00:35:44,400
pacified the farmers very well.

750
00:35:44,560 --> 00:35:47,220
Attorney Li, how about you go talk to them again?

751
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:48,000
Sure.

752
00:35:48,560 --> 00:35:50,400
Could it be that these farmers

753
00:35:50,400 --> 00:35:52,460
got a taste of the benefits last year,

754
00:35:52,800 --> 00:35:54,360
and their appetite has grown this year,

755
00:35:54,360 --> 00:35:56,040
so they deliberately killed those shrimp

756
00:35:56,040 --> 00:35:57,240
to ask us for money?

757
00:35:57,360 --> 00:35:58,360
Is this possible?

758
00:35:58,480 --> 00:36:00,280
We can't rule out this possibility.

759
00:36:00,280 --> 00:36:01,040
But right now,

760
00:36:01,040 --> 00:36:03,100
the M&A negotiation with Nanfu Group

761
00:36:03,320 --> 00:36:04,520
is the top priority.

762
00:36:04,720 --> 00:36:05,720
My suggestion is

763
00:36:05,880 --> 00:36:08,480
to run tests first and control public opinion.

764
00:36:08,600 --> 00:36:10,080
It's more efficient

765
00:36:10,560 --> 00:36:12,240
than making baseless inferences.

766
00:36:12,240 --> 00:36:13,760
This is the key point.

767
00:36:14,080 --> 00:36:15,560
We are not afraid of lawsuits.

768
00:36:15,560 --> 00:36:16,280
What we are afraid of is

769
00:36:16,280 --> 00:36:18,400
public opinion ruining our reputation.

770
00:36:18,400 --> 00:36:20,880
This M&A is very important.

771
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:22,440
Once the merger is successful,

772
00:36:22,440 --> 00:36:23,320
our Wangang

773
00:36:23,600 --> 00:36:26,720
will see a multi-billion expansion.

774
00:36:26,720 --> 00:36:28,580
So we must be extremely cautious.

775
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:32,000
I heard the one representing the farmers

776
00:36:32,040 --> 00:36:34,400
is that Xiao Longnv from last year.

777
00:36:34,600 --> 00:36:35,200
Yes.

778
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:36,360
Last year, she even sued one of our

779
00:36:36,360 --> 00:36:37,960
distributors named Hu.

780
00:36:38,200 --> 00:36:39,730
She's not easy to deal with.

781
00:36:39,800 --> 00:36:40,440
Lawyer Li.

782
00:36:40,560 --> 00:36:41,760
I'll have to trouble you

783
00:36:41,760 --> 00:36:43,440
to take care of this matter.

784
00:36:43,840 --> 00:36:45,640
We need to resolve this quickly.

785
00:36:45,640 --> 00:36:47,880
It's best if they withdraw the lawsuit.

786
00:36:51,760 --> 00:36:53,760
Do you have too much money and nowhere to spend it?

787
00:36:53,760 --> 00:36:56,490
You have some money burning a hole in your pocket.

788
00:36:56,560 --> 00:36:57,400
You could do anything else.

789
00:36:57,400 --> 00:36:58,640
But you want to invest in our law firm.

790
00:36:58,640 --> 00:37:00,500
Look at you, are you really not...

791
00:37:00,640 --> 00:37:02,640
What? Doubting my sincerity?

792
00:37:02,640 --> 00:37:04,120
Don't overthink it.

793
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:07,200
I just feel this is too sudden.

794
00:37:07,680 --> 00:37:09,360
She treated you well back then.

795
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:10,720
She took good care of you.

796
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:11,920
I poached you away.

797
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,400
So she must be feeling upset.

798
00:37:13,400 --> 00:37:15,440
Yes, I thought I'd inject some capital into her firm.

799
00:37:15,440 --> 00:37:17,760
If she does well, she'll remember your kindness.

800
00:37:17,760 --> 00:37:19,690
And if you do well, I do well, right?

801
00:37:19,760 --> 00:37:22,200
No wonder you can handle this massive wealth.

802
00:37:22,200 --> 00:37:24,400
You deserve to be the boss. You totally deserve it.

803
00:37:24,400 --> 00:37:25,480
Say no more.

804
00:37:25,880 --> 00:37:27,200
Good brothers for a lifetime.

805
00:37:27,200 --> 00:37:27,840
Two lifetimes.

806
00:37:27,840 --> 00:37:28,520
Three lifetimes.

807
00:37:28,520 --> 00:37:29,160
Four lifetimes.

808
00:37:29,160 --> 00:37:29,760
Five lifetimes.

809
00:37:29,760 --> 00:37:30,480
Six lifetimes.

810
00:37:30,480 --> 00:37:31,680
Then I'm going all in.

811
00:37:48,440 --> 00:37:49,440
Hu is back.

812
00:37:49,760 --> 00:37:51,680
You've really upgraded. You've made it.

813
00:37:51,680 --> 00:37:52,640
Call him Mr. Dong.

814
00:37:52,640 --> 00:37:53,520
Mr. Dong, Mr. Dong.

815
00:37:53,520 --> 00:37:54,360
How's business?

816
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:54,920
Not bad, not bad.

817
00:37:54,920 --> 00:37:55,600
Not bad.

818
00:37:59,840 --> 00:38:00,960
Godmother.

819
00:38:04,200 --> 00:38:05,480
Dali.

820
00:38:06,720 --> 00:38:07,800
It really is you.

821
00:38:07,800 --> 00:38:08,730
I came to see you.

822
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,280
You're too kind.

823
00:38:10,360 --> 00:38:12,080
My goodness, let me look at you.

824
00:38:12,080 --> 00:38:13,960
You look so different from when you were a kid.

825
00:38:13,960 --> 00:38:14,560
Am I handsome?

826
00:38:14,560 --> 00:38:15,200
Handsome.

827
00:38:17,360 --> 00:38:19,160
Look at Huzi now, looking so tough.

828
00:38:19,160 --> 00:38:20,090
Awesome, right?

829
00:38:20,400 --> 00:38:21,400
Awesome.

830
00:38:21,560 --> 00:38:23,400
Thanks for taking care of him.

831
00:38:24,080 --> 00:38:25,560
Did you pay him?

832
00:38:25,560 --> 00:38:26,600
What do you mean, pay him?

833
00:38:26,600 --> 00:38:28,640
Don't talk nonsense. We have business to attend to.

834
00:38:28,640 --> 00:38:30,360
We're going to visit his former boss.

835
00:38:30,360 --> 00:38:31,640
Going to see Lawyer Xiao, right?

836
00:38:31,640 --> 00:38:33,700
Make sure you introduce me properly.

837
00:38:38,120 --> 00:38:38,720
Uncle.

838
00:38:39,200 --> 00:38:40,440
Looking good, Mr. Dong.

839
00:38:40,440 --> 00:38:41,920
Suit and tie, very handsome.

840
00:38:41,920 --> 00:38:43,840
Of course. You kidding?

841
00:38:43,840 --> 00:38:44,160
How about that?

842
00:38:44,160 --> 00:38:45,040
You have a bodyguard now?

843
00:38:45,040 --> 00:38:47,280
What bodyguard? I'm his bodyguard.

844
00:38:47,440 --> 00:38:48,000
No.

845
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:50,120
This is my boss and my childhood friend,

846
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:51,400
Sun Zhuoli. No, no, no.

847
00:38:51,560 --> 00:38:52,360
Wan Zhuoli.

848
00:38:52,800 --> 00:38:55,000
And this is the director of our law firm, Xiao Longnv.

849
00:38:55,000 --> 00:38:56,320
Attorney Xiao, I've heard so much about you.

850
00:38:56,320 --> 00:38:57,680
Hello, Mr. Wan.

851
00:38:58,360 --> 00:38:59,000
This is great.

852
00:38:59,000 --> 00:39:00,560
Justice of Sword.

853
00:39:03,200 --> 00:39:04,800
What? It's Sword of Justice.

854
00:39:05,080 --> 00:39:06,080
No, don't we read it backwards?

855
00:39:06,080 --> 00:39:07,200
Read it forwards.

856
00:39:08,400 --> 00:39:10,880
That's great. It hasn't changed.

857
00:39:11,640 --> 00:39:13,200
Young man, have a cigar.

858
00:39:13,480 --> 00:39:14,000
Smoke it. Come on.

859
00:39:14,000 --> 00:39:15,120
Let your uncle cut it for you. Come on.

860
00:39:15,120 --> 00:39:15,960
No, no, no.

861
00:39:16,040 --> 00:39:18,480
Smoking is not allowed here. Don't you know?

862
00:39:18,480 --> 00:39:19,320
Isn't this a cigar?

863
00:39:19,320 --> 00:39:21,240
Is a cigar not a smoke? Doesn't it produce smoke?

864
00:39:21,240 --> 00:39:22,520
Then take it outside and smoke it yourself.

865
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:24,120
I don't smoke either, Uncle.

866
00:39:26,640 --> 00:39:27,370
Lawyer Xiao.

867
00:39:27,600 --> 00:39:29,280
I heard you like to drink.

868
00:39:29,280 --> 00:39:31,480
I specially picked this bottle for you.

869
00:39:31,600 --> 00:39:33,560
It's just a small token of my appreciation. Please accept it.

870
00:39:33,560 --> 00:39:34,920
But I'm afraid I'm not used to it.

871
00:39:34,920 --> 00:39:36,840
I usually just drink beer.

872
00:39:36,840 --> 00:39:38,280
It's very expensive. Just take it.

873
00:39:38,280 --> 00:39:40,200
I wouldn't even bear to spit it out after drinking it.

874
00:39:40,200 --> 00:39:41,840
Making such a big fuss.

875
00:39:42,040 --> 00:39:44,080
Do you have something to ask of me, Mr. Wan?

876
00:39:44,080 --> 00:39:45,080
Do you have a case?

877
00:39:46,120 --> 00:39:48,120
It's not a case. It's a partnership.

878
00:39:48,280 --> 00:39:49,560
It's a great opportunity.

879
00:39:49,560 --> 00:39:51,560
Huzi has been praising you to me,

880
00:39:51,720 --> 00:39:54,040
saying you are very capable and excellent.

881
00:39:54,040 --> 00:39:55,200
I was thinking,

882
00:39:55,200 --> 00:39:56,640
such an excellent lawyer like you

883
00:39:56,640 --> 00:39:58,480
shouldn't be buried on this street.

884
00:39:58,480 --> 00:40:00,400
Then what do you mean, Mr. Wan?

885
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:01,920
Where should I be buried?

886
00:40:04,120 --> 00:40:04,800
Humorous.

887
00:40:05,480 --> 00:40:07,920
I mean, I want to invest in your law firm.

888
00:40:08,520 --> 00:40:09,640
If we partner up,

889
00:40:09,880 --> 00:40:11,760
you just focus on going to court and handling cases,

890
00:40:11,760 --> 00:40:13,090
and leave the rest to me.

891
00:40:13,480 --> 00:40:15,360
I will first move this law firm

892
00:40:15,360 --> 00:40:16,690
out of this shabby place

893
00:40:16,920 --> 00:40:18,120
to the CBD.

894
00:40:18,120 --> 00:40:19,160
Rent an office building.

895
00:40:19,160 --> 00:40:20,720
We'll rent a whole floor.

896
00:40:21,240 --> 00:40:23,160
If we need people, just hire them.

897
00:40:23,160 --> 00:40:24,640
You're the boss. You call the shots.

898
00:40:24,640 --> 00:40:26,680
I'll get you a marketing team then.

899
00:40:26,680 --> 00:40:27,960
The most expensive kind.

900
00:40:27,960 --> 00:40:29,120
Promote it everywhere online,

901
00:40:29,120 --> 00:40:31,920
and make our law firm famous.

902
00:40:32,480 --> 00:40:34,080
That must cost a lot of money.

903
00:40:34,760 --> 00:40:35,400
Money?

904
00:40:35,400 --> 00:40:37,600
What money? Dali said,

905
00:40:37,600 --> 00:40:39,200
as long as it supports the legal cause,

906
00:40:39,200 --> 00:40:40,460
money doesn't matter.

907
00:40:40,480 --> 00:40:43,040
I'm telling you, this is a good opportunity. Seize it.

908
00:40:43,040 --> 00:40:44,520
Yes, it is a good opportunity.

909
00:40:44,520 --> 00:40:46,600
Since Mr. Wan supports the legal cause so much,

910
00:40:46,600 --> 00:40:47,720
what can our small law firm

911
00:40:47,720 --> 00:40:49,440
do to repay you?

912
00:40:51,640 --> 00:40:52,640
Here's the thing.

913
00:40:53,280 --> 00:40:54,680
I heard our law firm

914
00:40:54,840 --> 00:40:57,040
has recently been helping a farmer with a lawsuit.

915
00:40:57,040 --> 00:40:58,080
Is that true?

916
00:41:02,520 --> 00:41:04,640
Then let me ask you a question, Mr. Wan.

917
00:41:04,640 --> 00:41:07,880
Is your 'Wan' the same as in Wangang?

918
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:12,240
What a coincidence.

919
00:41:13,320 --> 00:41:15,720
You're going to sue Wangang?

920
00:41:16,000 --> 00:41:17,680
Mr. Dong, this is your fault.

921
00:41:17,680 --> 00:41:19,120
You have such a powerful childhood friend,

922
00:41:19,120 --> 00:41:20,280
why didn't you say so earlier?

923
00:41:20,280 --> 00:41:21,840
Why are you staying in my small company?

924
00:41:21,840 --> 00:41:24,360
You should have joined your friend a long time ago.

925
00:41:24,360 --> 00:41:25,000
It's fine.

926
00:41:25,720 --> 00:41:27,650
Now that we're all on the same page,

927
00:41:27,800 --> 00:41:29,800
we can have a good talk, right?

928
00:41:29,800 --> 00:41:30,730
Talk about what?

929
00:41:31,400 --> 00:41:33,200
About withdrawing the lawsuit?

930
00:41:36,680 --> 00:41:37,520
No wonder

931
00:41:37,760 --> 00:41:39,720
Mr. Wan suddenly got interested.

932
00:41:39,720 --> 00:41:42,760
You want to invest in my small law firm?

933
00:41:42,920 --> 00:41:43,760
Ms. Xiao.

934
00:41:44,400 --> 00:41:46,060
Our cooperation is a win-win.

935
00:41:46,560 --> 00:41:48,480
Your law firm can grow,

936
00:41:48,680 --> 00:41:49,800
and Wangang

937
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:51,800
can avoid some unnecessary trouble.

938
00:41:51,800 --> 00:41:52,860
Don't you think so?

939
00:41:53,080 --> 00:41:54,680
I don't understand, Mr. Wan.

940
00:41:55,320 --> 00:41:57,400
My client was treated unfairly.

941
00:41:57,600 --> 00:41:58,920
He wants to defend his rights.

942
00:41:58,920 --> 00:42:00,400
How is that trouble?

943
00:42:00,400 --> 00:42:01,640
There must be a misunderstanding.

944
00:42:01,640 --> 00:42:04,120
Ms. Xiao, don't be in a hurry to refuse me.

945
00:42:04,520 --> 00:42:05,480
Take your time to think about it.

946
00:42:05,480 --> 00:42:06,840
We can negotiate the terms.

947
00:42:06,840 --> 00:42:08,000
You are very busy.

948
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:10,520
So you might not be familiar with the law.

949
00:42:10,760 --> 00:42:12,240
Let me explain it to you.

950
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:14,760
If we keep talking, it means you're trying to bribe the opposing lawyer.

951
00:42:14,760 --> 00:42:15,960
This is illegal.

952
00:42:16,520 --> 00:42:18,580
If we continue, you'll need a lawyer.

953
00:42:19,480 --> 00:42:21,880
That would be very ugly, right?

954
00:42:22,640 --> 00:42:23,920
As for this wine,

955
00:42:25,200 --> 00:42:26,800
I really can't get used to it.

956
00:42:26,960 --> 00:42:29,360
Please take this expensive wine and leave.

957
00:42:32,080 --> 00:42:33,000
Why didn't you tell me

958
00:42:33,000 --> 00:42:35,520
that Ms. Xiao doesn't like to accept toasts?

959
00:42:36,680 --> 00:42:37,840
No, let's...

960
00:42:37,840 --> 00:42:38,920
Let's not be so tense, okay?

961
00:42:38,920 --> 00:42:39,840
Miao, see the guests out.

962
00:42:39,840 --> 00:42:42,440
I think there must be a misunderstanding here.

963
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:43,880
After you.

964
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:48,760
Dali.

965
00:42:52,080 --> 00:42:54,080
I didn't know he was going to talk about this.

966
00:42:54,080 --> 00:42:56,040
Let's go, Mr. Dong.
